    "Several leading tobacco companies announced today that they intend to sell crack cocaine as a new revenue source, in light of the $145 billion damage award against the tobacco industry in a recent Florida class-action lawsuit. The suit was brought by thousands of non-English speaking recent immigrant smokers who claimed they weren't aware of the health warnings that have been printed (in English) on every cigarette pack sold in North America since the 1960s, and the $145 billion verdict in favor of the plaintiffs is one of the largest judgments to date against the tobacco companies.": "",
    "Something that people are willing to pay serious money for, with few questions asked, in a market that is currently not well served by suppliers, despite the existence of a huge supply, especially in poor, Third World countries. We have done a lot of spade work, and find that the best way to go about this is to set up an independent auction site on the floating \"city\" in international waters, in the North Sea. That offshore site, which seems ideal for our purposes, is the place where a number of controversial activities such as human cloning, brain transplants, genetic experiments": "",
    "Teams of police and military personnel, dressed in anticontamination \"spacesuits,\" picked through the wreckage of downtown London yesterday, looking for clues, in the wake of the greatest catastrophe in that venerable city's history. Unknown terrorists are believed to have set off the series of massive explosions at rush hour Monday afternoon, which completely devastated several main London subway tunnels and stations. The blasts were apparently timed to coincide with the release of deadly toxic nerve gas at numerous key points throughout the downtown areas of the subway system.": "",
