    "Ever since the big flap over inserting genetic material from swine into grapefruit, which had some nasty repercussions once the secret got out (especially among the Jewish and Muslim communities, and among vegetarians), it has been very difficult for supermarkets to overcome consumer resistance to genetically modified foods. We practically have to give the stuff away, in order to move it off the shelves. The only thing harder to sell is the \"embalmed\" (irradiated) stuff, which doesn't glow in the dark, but is full of all kinds of \"unique\" chemicals caused by the irradiation.": "",
