    "These two are yet more examples of the large number of high-ranking financial executives and a Governor of the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas who have either committed suicide, died under somewhat suspicious circumstances, or simply vanished recently. In the most sensational of these occurrences, the Dallas Fed Governor's half-eaten body was found in the lion enclosure in the Fort Worth zoo. Fort Worth police said foul play was not suspected, however.": "",
    "....Meanwhile, in related business news, a spokesman for the American Petroleum Institute says that the future has never looked brighter for the energy industry, since the opening of the Alaska Wildlife Reserve to oil drilling and for strip mining of coal. Referring to the recent warm winters and almost tropical summers in Alaska, he noted that \"...Even Mother Nature herself seems to be aiding our exploration and development activities in Alaska....\"": "",
    "The fanatical fundamentalist cult, once thought to have been virtually stamped out when Utah and federal law enforcement arrested and convicted their leader and drove them out of their enclave along the Utah/Arizona border, took refuge in west Texas and has been growing like an oil slick ever since, attracting many older males who were lured into membership by the prospect of church-arranged marriages to young brides, some as young as nine years old.": "",
    "The U.S. Seventh Fleet, which began steaming in the direction of the Korean Peninsula within minutes after the war began yesterday morning, was recalled after today's nuclear incident, and after a warning from the Supreme Leader of North Korea that North Korea had targeted Los Angeles and San Francisco with nuclear missiles that would be fired immediately, if the American fleet attempted to attack North Korea, or undo its \"liberation\" of South Korea.": "",
    "Despite a massive death toll from the highly contagious Hainan Virus, Chinese authorites say that drastic quarantine measures have succeeded in confining the lethal new virus to the island of Hainan, and that the virus appears to have burned itself out, and is now under control, while clean-up crews in hazmat suits continue disposing of thousands of bodies in mass funeral pyres and spraying every inch of the large island with chemical disinfectants.": "",
    "Several major U.S. personnel agencies were said to already be looking into ways to take advantage of the new \"free labor market\" (pro-slavery) legislation, and in Chicago, one of the principal commodity exchanges is rumored to be readying new futures contracts for indentured services, now that former prohibitions on buying and selling the rights to forced labor have been effectively removed from the U.S. constitution by an activist Supreme Court....": "",
    "We have been offered a lucrative proposition, involving the sale of customer information. As a security firm, we are of course privy to a lot of highly important information that our customers and clients entrust to us, to enable us to do our job properly, such as passwords and entry codes for customers' facilities, plus detailed technical information on safes and other equipment our customers have installed to maintain the security of their assets.": "",
    "Officials at Interpol had no comment on this strange skein of untimely deaths and disappearances of highprofile bank and mortgage company executives. An FBI official told CNN that there was \"... nothing out of the ordinary going on here. **** happens. Anyone who says these events are somehow related to the fact that all these guys are involved in the subprime mortgage securities business, which is booming, is just a lunatic conspiracy theorist....\"": "",
    "The virus, a notorious \"Trojan Horse\"-type virus, was disseminated widely by a team of young hackers that the company allegedly installed in a posh beachside mansion near Negril Beach, in Jamaica. The young hackers, who were supplied with unlimited cola drinks, junk food, and computer games, were also paid large bonuses based on the number of competitors' servers they could bring down by means of coordinated denial of service attacks by the virus.": "",
    "We will need to fire our stuffy, conservative old investment firm that has managed the pension plan investments up till now, of course, since there is no way the Plan can earn 9.5% a year on the stodgy kinds of things they have been investing in. Our stockbrokers have recommended an aggressive money management firm that has a great track record, and says they can earn AT LEAST 20% a year returns for us if we let them manage the Pension Plan funds.": "",
    "\"mountain of copper\" at a remote rainforest location in Indonesia's Irian Jaya. The company, upon beginning mining operations in the area, after several pitched battles with local headhunters (which cost the lives of 20 miners), quickly discovered that the \"mountain of copper\" they had bought had been heavily \"salted\" with high-grade copper ore by a group of brilliant con men who claimed they had made the greatest copper discovery in the world.": "",
    "In Mexico, rioting continues, as that government announced another major increase in the heavily subsidized price of corn and tortillas, staple items in the diet of that nation. In Canada, the trickle of refugees moving south, fleeing the bitter cold and growing ice sheet, has grown into a flood of late, prompting members of the U.S. Congress to call for building a fence or wall along the Canadian border to keep out the horde of hungry Canucks.": "",
    " officials said that an independent board monitoring a study for newly developed cholesterol treatment dranotrapib recommended that the work end because of an unexpected number of deaths and other complications. A senior resident physician at one large university medical center where the new drug was being tested was quoted in a television news broadcast as saying, \"Our patients in the test group for dranotrapib have been dying like flies....\"": "",
    "Without awaiting your approval, the Marketing and Product Development Group has taken the initiative and acquired the rights to a controversial new publication, authored by [DELETED FOR SECURITY REASONS]. We paid the author an advance of 10 million Swiss Francs, so we will have a bit of a write-off if you veto this project, and we recognized that risk, but felt this was too great an opportunity to let slip by, in case you decide to go with it.": "",
    "\"We will soon be opening a web site, based in Khartoum, in the Sudan, that will auction off slaves throughout North Africa and the Middle East. This is another huge market, currently underserved, and this time we are locating at the very heart of the supply area, with a highly scalable business strategy, so no one will be able to match our cost structure. This is a company on the go, and we are big enough to write off our mistakes and move on.": "",
    "The balance of power has shifted drastically in favor of the new Islamic State, which now dwarfs the U.S., Russia, or China in military assets and resources. Emissaries of all three former superpowers are currently in Cairo, with hats in hand, negotiating over the amount of annual tribute that will be paid to the Caliphate, in order to maintain peaceful relations with, and a steady flow of oil from, the new, and now sole, reigning superpower.": "",
