    "The drug is highly addictive, and it drastically lowers I.Q. and the capability for critical thinking, but it makes kids very passive, pliable, and far more willing to accept any kind of mind-numbing political indoctrination that may be promoted by the school administrators' political commissars, making it an ideal tool which has already been thoroughly tested with great results in government-run schools in Iran, Venezuela, and North Korea.": "",
    "Politicians in Washington these days have no honor. In the bad old days, when we bought a Congressman, he stayed bought. Now it's more like a lease, with annual rent increases. This year, we have a huge potential problem, with reform legislation pending in the Senate now that, if enacted, could erase all our special tax breaks and government subsidies, which have taken us years of prodigious lobbying efforts and suitcases of cash to attain.": "",
    "International tensions have grown, stretching good relations almost to the breaking point, following the U.S. withdrawal from and repudiation of almost all of its trade agreements, and the enactment by the U.S. Congress of heavy tariffs on most kinds of imported goods. This has led to a chain reaction of retaliatory tariffs and other non-tariff trade barriers being erected by a number of European countries, Canada, Mexico, and much of Asia.": "",
    "Even the CIA, IRS and other government agencies are reported to be having trouble keeping up their usual levels of importation of \"Colombian nose candy\" through various officially-sanctioned channels in recent weeks, which is having dire consequences on those agencies' operating budgets. Congress, in special session, is considering emergency agricultural aid to Colombia's devastated coca farmers until the flow of \"ghetto sedatives\" resumes.": "",
